# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere (with byte-preserved exceptions).
#
# All text is normalized to LF in the repo and on checkout, on every OS. This
# ends the recurring CRLF<->LF churn: app/, components/, and lib/ were previously
# left as CRLF, which kept the worktree perpetually dirty, inflated diffs, and
# made copy/paste carry stray carriage returns.
#
# Apply ONCE, on a CLEAN tree (no uncommitted content edits):
#   git config core.autocrlf false
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "normalize line endings to LF tree-wide; end CRLF/LF churn"

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Byte-preserved, checksum-bound: NEVER normalize (SHA-256 would break) ---
# The historical source museum is byte-exact and its SHA-256 is recorded/verified.
public/artifacts/source-lineage/** -text

# --- Binary assets: never normalize ---
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.mdb   binary
*.dbf   binary
*.cdx   binary

# SVG and generated provenance sidecars are text -> LF (explicit for clarity).
*.svg                   text eol=lf
*.svg.provenance.json   text eol=lf
